WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.667
The recent-activity view publishes completed transactions from a defined six-month window.

00:00:05.667 --> 00:00:09.997
That shared definition can support multiple retention analyses.

00:00:09.997 --> 00:00:17.407
It creates a smaller, clearer interface than asking every report author to repeat the transaction-status

00:00:17.407 --> 00:00:22.722
logic. A standard view stores a query definition, not a separate copy of the rows.

00:00:22.722 --> 00:00:29.832
Treat the selected columns, names, types, and grain as a contract with downstream users.

00:00:29.832 --> 00:00:36.317
Changing that contract can break dashboards or applications even if the underlying query still runs.
